  + recognized anchors are caller-supplied bindings
  + call identity, inference job identity, and pass index are caller-supplied correlation
  + Cantor derives receipts, hashes, lane evidence, schema, proposal, and argument digest under existing fake experiment rules
  + preparation does not make the candidate true, safe, signed by a real authority, provider-generated, or production-admitted

& [DualHemisphereReview] converges
  + [expansive] one prepare operation makes the subprocess seam usable from any JSON-capable controller
  + [constraining] automated construction could appear to mint trust unless the response preserves fixture-grade principals and explicit residuals
  + [synthesis] add prepare as an additive profile, refuse invalid candidates, and keep base schema run verify bytes unchanged

